---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-klaviyo';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS vs Klaviyo for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Retain review and loyalty context when moving messaging to Klaviyo.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS today?",
    "answer": "Yotpo states that the application is decommissioned. This is now a migration decision, separate from retaining its Reviews or Loyalty products."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "Yes. Yotpo documents a Klaviyo Reviews integration. Decide whether invitations are sent through the documented Klaviyo trigger or the reviews service, and prevent duplicate requests."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does loyalty data transfer automatically with email contacts?",
    "answer": "Do not assume it does. Configure the separate Loyalty integration and inspect the actual properties and events received before enabling reward messages."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should every old flow be recreated?",
    "answer": "No. Rebuild flows that still have a business purpose and valid entry data. Historical orders should not become new welcome or review entries simply because records were imported."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I export from the retired account now?",
    "answer": "Do not assume access remains available. Use records already retained and ask the relevant support teams about missing data; this page promises no recovery or export access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also evaluate Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "You can include Sequenzy in the email shortlist. Verify the required Shopify events, suppression, consent handling and current commercial terms before choosing it; it is not assumed to replace SMS or review infrastructure."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Yotpo Email & SMS vs Klaviyo</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Migration comparison · reviewed November 24, 2026</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Klaviyo for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Retain review and loyalty context when moving messaging to Klaviyo. Yotpo confirms that Email &amp; SMS has been decommissioned. This page evaluates a replacement workflow, not a trial of two currently available senders.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Separate the retired sender from the remaining modules</h2>
        <p>Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty are separate from the retired Email & SMS sender. Keeping a review widget does not require keeping that sender. Inventory who owns review invitations, points notifications and marketing before rebuilding flows; replacing all Yotpo products at once can turn a messaging migration into a much larger project.</p>
        <h2>Review eligibility is different from an order event</h2>
        <p>Yotpo documents an Eligible for Yotpo Review Request trigger for Klaviyo and reviewer properties on mutual contacts. Use the eligibility event for the review invitation if that is your chosen ownership model. A generic order event does not establish that a review is due. Avoid running a second invitation from the reviews service for the same purchase.</p>
        <h2>Rebuild loyalty messages from documented fields</h2>
        <p>The Yotpo Loyalty integration pushes program data into Klaviyo. Record the actual property and event names available in your account before writing points or tier copy. A stored points balance is not proof that a new tier event occurred, and an old balance should not be rendered as a current reward promise. Define missing-data fallbacks rather than showing blank or stale benefits.</p>
        <h2>Proposed jewelry-store acceptance scenario</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical jewelry store, create a controlled order with a gift recipient different from the buyer. Keep the invitation attached to the correct buyer identity and eligible product, and verify how a return affects the planned follow-up. Then submit a review and confirm that any reviewer-status branch receives the expected update. These are proposed checks, not observed merchant results.</p>
        <h2>Cart proof and winback need different inputs</h2>
        <p>A review invitation integration does not automatically provide approved customer images for every carted SKU. Check content permissions, product matching and fallback blocks separately. For winback, distinguish observed purchase history from a predictive field and inspect eligibility for that field in the actual account; do not migrate an old predictive segment as if it were a static customer tag.</p>
        <h2>Cutover and operating cost</h2>
        <p>Keep old flow definitions as reference if already retained, but do not replay historical orders into live welcome or review flows. Review active profile counts, email volume, SMS destinations and retained Yotpo modules in the quote. The relevant cost includes maintaining event mappings and invitation ownership, rather than a claim that either vendor universally saves operator hours.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits</h2>
        <p>If you are considering Sequenzy for email, compare the same required events, exclusions and operating tasks before selecting it. Confirm current Shopify integration scope and pricing directly. Do not assume it replaces the SMS sender, review collection or loyalty service.</p>
        <h2>Primary evidence and limits</h2>
        <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. No live migration, deliverability experiment or merchant revenue test was performed. Current account eligibility, quotes and missing historical records remain to be confirmed.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommissioning notice</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://support.yotpo.com/docs/klaviyo-integration-guide">Yotpo Reviews integration guide</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://support.yotpo.com/docs/integrating-yotpo-loyalty-referrals-with-klaviyo">Yotpo Loyalty integration guide</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Klaviyo vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Yotpo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc">Reviews & UGC playbook</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Klaviyo FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
